    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d177-a1">

                <pb facs="0337" n="265" sameAs="frus:frus1882/pg265"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure in No. 52.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Frelinghuysen to
                        Mr. West</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State, Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1882-04-10"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >April</hi> 10, 1882</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Referring to my reply of the 28th ultimo to
                    your note of the 24th of that month, in relation to the imprisonment of a
                    British subject named William Lane, at Detroit, Mich., I now have the honor to
                    inform you that I have received a letter from the attorney-general of Michigan,
                    in which that officer states that the prisoner in question has been convicted of
                    an assault with intent to murder,</p>
                <p>I have, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>F. T. FRELINGHUYSEN.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
